{
  "$comment": "Design system of the agnos-perf-center page. Three tiers: global holds the only raw values; semantic names a role and refers to a global token, per theme when it is a colour; component refers to a semantic token. The generator writes semantic tokens as --s-<name> and component tokens as --c-<name>; the page's CSS and script use those only. History view: one colour per identity; the first twelve, by commits, are color.identity-1 to 12, chosen for at least 3:1 on the raised surface of both themes (indigo 500 rather than 600, which gives 2.84:1 on the dark one); the next ones are oklch hues turned by dimension.history-hue-step from dimension.history-hue-start, at the two history lightnesses and the history chroma (worst 3.44:1 on both themes). Git graph of a commit: eight branch colours per theme, taken in turn by the lanes, from hues other than the identities' order so that a lane is not read as a person. Brand: the five colours of the 'Spans' mark, with one value for both themes since a mark keeps its colours, and the tokens of the licence badges of the Help dialog: a slate label, an ink and four tones, the ink keeping at least 4.5:1 over each. The lockup of the About topic: the name's size, line height and tracking and the tagline's tracking and line height are the design's own values; its text colours are the semantic text and muted-text tokens, the design's greys (#181C22, #5A6472 and their dark variants) being a few points of lightness away from them. The legend's relation samples: graph-legend-edge-width takes stroke-medium (1.2px) rather than stroke-hairline (1px), the nearest existing step above it, for extra visibility at the sample's small size (owner's review, 2026-11-07); a dedicated step for the requested +25% was not added since it would sit a fraction of a pixel from stroke-medium. Dark theme in layers (owner's mock-up review, candidate P2, 2026-11-07): the dark-* surfaces grow lighter from fields to page, raised and hover, the raised one near the ceiling where marks keep 3:1; text-subtle (slate-450), type-ftr and type-task (lightened Okabe-Ito hues) border-strong (slate-550) and identities 1, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9 and 12 (one step lighter) take dark variants that deviate from their light value so as to keep 4.5:1 and 3:1 on every dark surface, which makes those seven identities per theme (amends); color.blue-900 takes Tailwind's own value, in place of the grade green copied by mistake.",
